+# Q4 Overflow Fulfillment Plan
+
+## Decision summary
+
+- Planning basis: Use the four-week base forecast, totaling 66,000 units against 48,000 units of baseline capacity. [Demand Forecast] [Capacity Note]
+- Chosen partner: Use Meridian Fulfillment for the external share of overflow because its proposed capacity accommodates the planned allocation. [Partner Sheet]
+- Corrected allocation: Route 75% of each week’s overflow to Meridian and 25% to internal overtime.
+
+## Sourced facts
+
+| Fact | Evidence type | Source |
+|---|---|---|
+| Standard fulfillment capacity is 12,000 shipped units per week, based on the average of eight steady-state weeks. | Observed | [Capacity Note] |
+| Base forecasts are 14,400 units for 2026-11-02, 16,800 for 2026-11-09, 19,200 for 2026-11-16, and 15,600 for 2026-11-23. | Forecast | [Demand Forecast] |
+| Internal overtime is limited to 2,000 incremental units per week and costs $3.10 per unit. | Operating limit | [Capacity Note] |
+| The August pilot processed 1,500 incremental units with 96.2% same-day completion; it was a single non-holiday pilot. | Observed | [Capacity Note] |
+| Meridian offers 6,000 units of weekly capacity at $2.40 per unit plus a one-time $1,500 setup fee. | Proposal term | [Partner Sheet] |
+| Meridian projects 98.0% ship-on-time if product mix matches the forecast and complete order files arrive by 18:00 on the prior day. | Supplier projection | [Partner Sheet] |
+
+## Recommendation
+
+We recommend reserving Meridian and applying the corrected allocation consistently to each week’s calculated overflow. Across the window, forecast demand exceeds baseline capacity by 18,000 units: Meridian would receive 13,500 and overtime would absorb 4,500. [Demand Forecast] [Capacity Note] This balances Meridian’s proposed external handling rate against the operational usefulness of retaining an internal share. [Partner Sheet] [Capacity Note] These facts support the recommendation but remain distinct from it.
+
+The tightest point is the week of 2026-11-16. Meridian’s 5,400-unit allocation leaves 600 units below its proposed weekly limit, while the 1,800-unit overtime allocation leaves 200 units below the internal limit. [Demand Forecast] [Capacity Note] [Partner Sheet] That is capacity headroom, not a guarantee that actual mix, file quality, or execution will conform to the plan.
+
+## Weekly allocation
+
+The figures below subtract the 12,000-unit baseline from each base forecast, then apply the corrected split. [Demand Forecast] [Capacity Note]
+
+| Week of | Forecast units | Baseline capacity | Overflow | Meridian (75%) | Overtime (25%) |
+|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
+| 2026-11-02 | 14,400 | 12,000 | 2,400 | 1,800 | 600 |
+| 2026-11-09 | 16,800 | 12,000 | 4,800 | 3,600 | 1,200 |
+| 2026-11-16 | 19,200 | 12,000 | 7,200 | 5,400 | 1,800 |
+| 2026-11-23 | 15,600 | 12,000 | 3,600 | 2,700 | 900 |
+| Total | 66,000 | 48,000 | 18,000 | 13,500 | 4,500 |
+
+## Cost estimate
+
+The estimate applies Meridian’s proposal terms and the internal overtime rate to the allocated units. [Partner Sheet] [Capacity Note]
+
+| Item | Amount |
+|---|---:|
+| Meridian handling | $32,400.00 |
+| Meridian setup | $1,500.00 |
+| Overtime handling | $13,950.00 |
+| Total incremental cost | $47,850.00 |
+
+Excluded costs are returns, rework, and downstream freight because reliable estimates are unavailable. [Capacity Note] The total is therefore an incremental handling estimate, not a complete landed-cost forecast.
+
+## Uncertainty
+
+- Uncertainty: The demand values are forecasts, not booked orders. [Demand Forecast] [Capacity Note] Impact: Actual overflow and both allocations may differ, especially in the peak week. Recommended response: Refresh volumes weekly and recalculate the same corrected split before releasing work.
+- Uncertainty: Meridian’s 98.0% figure is a supplier projection conditioned on product mix and timely complete files, and Northstar Home has no live history with the partner. [Partner Sheet] Impact: Ship-on-time performance could differ from the proposal. Recommended response: Send the requested test file, monitor daily results, and use remaining stated headroom if variance emerges.
+- Uncertainty: Returns, rework, and downstream freight lack reliable estimates. [Capacity Note] Impact: The $47,850.00 estimate understates the full financial exposure if those costs occur. Recommended response: Track these categories separately and update the estimate when evidence becomes available.
+
+## Actions
+
+1. Reserve the four weekly Meridian allocations and confirm proposal terms. Owner: Fulfillment lead. Due: 2026-10-16.
+2. Deliver and validate the requested test order file. Owner: Order systems lead. Due: 2026-10-23.
+3. Confirm overtime staffing for each weekly allocation. Owner: Site operations manager. Due: 2026-10-26.
+4. Publish the first weekly forecast refresh and variance view. Owner: Demand planning lead. Due: 2026-10-30.
